        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Waikiki",
            "zh": "威基基"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", Hawaii, is known around the world for its beautiful beaches. On April 14, a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Hawaiian monk seal",
            "zh": "夏威夷僧海豹"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " gave birth to her fifth child on one of the beaches. The 12-year-old seal is named Kaiwi. She and her baby seal will stay on the beach for about two months. During this time, Kaiwi will carefully care for and "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "nurture",
            "ref": "v-nurture"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " her young baby there until it is strong enough to live alone."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The Hawaiian monk seal is the most "
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "endangered"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " seal "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "species",
            "ref": "v-species"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in US "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "waters",
            "zh": "水域"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". There are fewer than 1,600 of them living in the world today. To protect Kaiwi and her newborn baby, Hawaiian officials have closed off the beach where they are resting. A "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "temporary",
            "ref": "v-temporary"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "fence",
            "ref": "v-fence"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " has been "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "erected",
            "ref": "v-erect"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " around part of the beach to keep people away. And guards have been "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "patrolling",
            "zh": "巡逻"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the beach area and nearby waters "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "day and night",
            "ref": "v-day-and-night"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to ensure their safety."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Some tourists visiting Waikiki are upset about the closure of part of the beach. But most of them understand and support the officials’ decision. “After all, the beach belongs not only to us humans, but also to all other animals,” said one visitor. Many people feel happy to see the mother seal and her baby being protected in their natural home."
          }
        ]
      },
